+# tensor\_filter ara2
+
+## Overview
+
+The `ara2` sub-plugin connects NNStreamer's `tensor_filter` element to the
+Ara-2 NPU. It uses the tensor\_filter V2 invoke API, which enables
+DMA-BUF zero-copy: when the upstream element delivers a DMA-BUF buffer, the
+data is transferred to the NPU without any CPU memory copy.
+
+Communication with the NPU goes through a proxy daemon (`dvproxy`) over a
+Unix socket. The client library (`libaraclient_aarch64.so`) is loaded at
+runtime via `dlopen`, so the plugin degrades gracefully when the runtime is
+not installed.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- Ara-2 NPU hardware connected to the host
+- `dvproxy` daemon running
+- `libaraclient_aarch64.so` in the dynamic linker path
+- `/dev/dma_heap/linux,cma` device available (for DMA-BUF allocation)
+- Model file in `.dvm` format compiled for the Ara-2
+
+## Build
+
+Enable the sub-plugin at configuration time:
+
+```
+meson setup build -Dara2-support=enabled
+ninja -C build
+sudo ninja -C build install
+```
+
+Detection is automatic: if the `dvapi.h` header is not found, the sub-plugin
+is silently skipped.
+
+## Pipeline usage
+
+**Basic:**
+```
+tensor_filter framework=ara2 model=model.dvm
+```
+
+**With custom properties:**
+```
+tensor_filter framework=ara2 model=model.dvm \
+    custom=SocketPath:/var/run/proxy.sock,Timeout:3000,EnableStats:true
+```
+
+## Custom properties
+
+Properties are passed as comma-separated `Key:Value` pairs to the `custom`
+property of `tensor_filter`.
+
+| Property | Default | Description |
+|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `SocketPath` | `/var/run/proxy.sock` | Unix socket path to the dvproxy daemon |
+| `Timeout` | `5000` | Inference timeout in milliseconds |
+| `EnableStats` | `false` | Enable periodic inference statistics logging |
+| `ZeroCopy` | `false` | Enable DMA-BUF zero-copy mode (see note below) |
+
+## Input/output format
+
+The sub-plugin queries the loaded model for its native tensor format
+(dimensions, data type) and reports it directly to NNStreamer. Upstream
+elements must deliver data in that exact format.
+
+For int8 models the upstream video converter must perform the actual
+value-range conversion (e.g. uint8 [0,255] → int8 [-128,127]). Use
+`tensor_converter input-type=int8` to confirm that the conversion has
+happened.
+
+## Zero-copy pipeline
+
+**Note:** DMA-BUF zero-copy is currently **disabled by default** due to known
+issues with output buffer reuse causing frozen bounding boxes in detection
+pipelines. Enable it explicitly with `ZeroCopy:true` only for testing or if
+your use case is not affected.
+
+When enabled and the upstream element supports buffer pool negotiation and
+delivers DMA-BUF memory, the ara2 sub-plugin bypasses all CPU copies:
+
+```
+v4l2src
+  ! video/x-raw,format=NV12
+  ! videoscale
+  ! video/x-raw,format=RGB,width=640,height=640
+  ! tensor_converter
+  ! tensor_filter framework=ara2 model=model.dvm custom=ZeroCopy:true
+  ! tensor_sink
+```
+
+Zero-copy is active when you see this log line (GST_DEBUG=tensor_filter:5):
+```
+Ara-2: DMA-BUF zero-copy enabled (input + output)
+ara2_invoke_v2 first frame: input_dmabuf=yes output_dmabuf=yes
+```
+
+If disabled (default), you will see:
+```
+Ara-2: Zero-copy disabled by ZeroCopy property. Using CPU memory mode.
+```
+
+For planar formats (RGBP/BGRP) the width must be a multiple of 4.
+
+## Quantization metadata
+
+The sub-plugin attaches `GstNnsTensorQuantMeta` to each output buffer
+when the model reports per-tensor quantization parameters (scale and
+zero-point). Downstream decoders can read this metadata to dequantize
+output tensors without hardcoded parameters.
+
+## Fallback behaviour
+
+If DMA-BUF is not available (e.g. videotestsrc pipeline) the sub-plugin
+falls back to system memory automatically. The log will show:
+```
+ara2_invoke_v2 first frame: input_dmabuf=no output_dmabuf=yes
+```
+
+## Debugging
+
+```bash
+# Verbose ara2 and converter logging
+GST_DEBUG=ara2:5,tensor_converter:5,tensor_filter:4 gst-launch-1.0 ...
+
+# Check DMA heap availability
+ls -l /dev/dma_heap/
+
+# Check dvproxy is running
+pgrep dvproxy
+```
+
+## Known limitations
+
+- Multi-tensor input DMA-BUF is not supported.
+- Flexible tensor format (`num_tensors == 0`) is not supported.
+- Padding removal for RGBP/BGRP is not supported in the DMA-BUF path.
