+# tensor\_filter V2 invoke API
+
+## Overview
+
+The V2 API (`GST_TENSOR_FILTER_FRAMEWORK_V2`) extends the existing V0/V1
+interfaces with DMA-BUF zero-copy support. Instead of receiving pre-mapped
+buffer pointers, a V2 sub-plugin receives opaque `GstMemory*` pointers and
+can inspect their type before deciding whether to map them in CPU or pass
+the underlying file descriptor directly to the hardware.
+
+V0 and V1 sub-plugins are unaffected; the dispatch layer detects the API
+version and routes accordingly.
+
+## When to use V2
+
+Use V2 when:
+- Your hardware can accept a DMA-BUF file descriptor directly (no CPU copy).
+- You want to advertise a hardware buffer pool to upstream elements so they
+  write into your device memory from the start.
+
+For all other cases, V1 is sufficient and simpler.
+
+## API version constant
+
+```c
+#define GST_TENSOR_FILTER_FRAMEWORK_V2  (GST_TENSOR_FILTER_FRAMEWORK_BASE | 0x20000ULL)
+```
+
+Set `GstTensorFilterFramework.version = GST_TENSOR_FILTER_FRAMEWORK_V2`.
+
+## New callbacks
+
+All new callbacks are placed in the `v2` sub-struct of
+`GstTensorFilterFramework`.
+
+### invoke_v2
+
+```c
+int (*invoke_v2) (const GstTensorFilterFramework *self,
+                  GstTensorFilterProperties *prop,
+                  void *private_data,
+                  void **input,   /* array of GstMemory* */
+                  void **output,  /* array of GstMemory* */
+                  guint num_input,
+                  guint num_output);
+```
+
+`input` and `output` are arrays of `GstMemory*` cast to `void*`. The
+sub-plugin must **not** call `gst_memory_map()` unless it needs CPU access.
+To detect DMA-BUF memory use `gst_is_dmabuf_memory(mem)` and retrieve the
+file descriptor with `gst_dmabuf_memory_get_fd(mem)`.
+
+The sub-plugin owns `output` memory: it must allocate output `GstMemory`
+objects (e.g. from its own DMA-BUF pool) and store them in `output[]`.
+The framework wraps them into the output `GstBuffer`.
+
+### propose_allocation
+
+```c
+int (*propose_allocation) (const GstTensorFilterFramework *self,
+                           GstTensorFilterProperties *prop,
+                           void *private_data,
+                           GstQuery *query);
+```
+
+Called when the upstream element sends a `GST_QUERY_ALLOCATION` downstream.
+The sub-plugin should add its DMA-BUF pool and/or allocator to `query` so
+that upstream allocates from the hardware buffer pool.
+
+`tensor_converter` forwards this query transparently from its sink to its
+source pad, so the pool proposal reaches the video converter upstream.
+
+### get_model_metadata (optional)
+
+```c
+const char *(*get_model_metadata) (const GstTensorFilterFramework *self,
+                                   GstTensorFilterProperties *prop,
+                                   void *private_data);
+```
+
+Return a JSON string describing model metadata (labels, task type, etc.).
+Return `NULL` if not supported.
+
+## Minimal V2 sub-plugin skeleton (C)
+
+```c
+static int
+my_invoke_v2 (const GstTensorFilterFramework *self,
+              GstTensorFilterProperties *prop, void *priv,
+              void **input, void **output,
+              guint num_in, guint num_out)
+{
+  GstMemory *in_mem = (GstMemory *) input[0];
+
+  if (gst_is_dmabuf_memory (in_mem)) {
+    int fd = gst_dmabuf_memory_get_fd (in_mem);
+    /* pass fd directly to hardware */
+  } else {
+    GstMapInfo map;
+    gst_memory_map (in_mem, &map, GST_MAP_READ);
+    /* copy map.data to hardware */
+    gst_memory_unmap (in_mem, &map);
+  }
+
+  /* allocate output and store in output[0] */
+  output[0] = (void *) gst_allocator_alloc (my_allocator, out_size, NULL);
+  /* run inference ... */
+  return 0;
+}
+
+static int
+my_propose_allocation (const GstTensorFilterFramework *self,
+                       GstTensorFilterProperties *prop, void *priv,
+                       GstQuery *query)
+{
+  gst_query_add_allocation_pool (query, my_pool, buf_size, min, max);
+  return 0;
+}
+
+static GstTensorFilterFramework my_fw = {
+  .version = GST_TENSOR_FILTER_FRAMEWORK_V2,
+  .name = "my_hw",
+  /* ... other fields ... */
+  .v2.invoke_v2 = my_invoke_v2,
+  .v2.propose_allocation = my_propose_allocation,
+};
+```
+
+## Reference implementation
+
+See `ext/nnstreamer/tensor_filter/tensor_filter_ara2.cc` for a complete V2
+C++ sub-plugin using DMA-BUF heap allocation, a three-tier invoke (zero-copy
+→ external DMA-BUF → CPU fallback), and a full propose_allocation
+implementation.
+
+## Compatibility
+
+- V0 and V1 sub-plugins continue to work without changes.
+- The framework detects the version from `GstTensorFilterFramework.version`
+  and dispatches accordingly.
+- A V2 sub-plugin is **not** required to handle DMA-BUF; it may also map all
+  memory with `gst_memory_map()` and behave identically to V1.
